; DNS for AI Discovery (DNS-AID)
; draft-mozleywilliams-dnsop-dnsaid + RFC 9460
;
; HOW TO USE
; 1. Replace every occurrence of EXAMPLE.COM with your apex domain
;    (custom domain under your DNS host — not *.vercel.app).
; 2. Publish these ServiceMode SVCB records at your DNS provider
;    (Cloudflare, Route 53, Google Cloud DNS, DNSimple, Vercel DNS, …).
; 3. Enable DNSSEC on the zone and publish the DS record at the registrar
;    so validating resolvers return AD=1 answers.
; 4. Verify:
;      dig +short SVCB _index._agents.EXAMPLE.COM @1.1.1.1
;      dig +dnssec SVCB _index._agents.EXAMPLE.COM @1.1.1.1
;
; Notes
; - TargetName MUST NOT contain underscores (TLS / public certs).
; - Prefer SVCB (type 64). Some scanners also accept HTTPS (type 65).
; - Do not invent unregistered named SvcParams (cap, endpoint, bap, …)
;   until IANA assigns numbers; use only registered keys (alpn, port, …).

; Organizational agent index (required well-known entrypoint)
_index._agents.EXAMPLE.COM. 300 IN SVCB 1 EXAMPLE.COM. (
    alpn="h2,h3"
    port=443
    mandatory=alpn,port
)

; Optional: same binding as HTTPS RR if your provider prefers type 65
; _index._agents.EXAMPLE.COM. 300 IN HTTPS 1 EXAMPLE.COM. alpn="h2,h3" port=443 mandatory=alpn,port

; Optional A2A leaf when you publish /.well-known/agent-card.json
; _a2a._agents.EXAMPLE.COM. 300 IN SVCB 1 EXAMPLE.COM. (
;     alpn="h2,h3"
;     port=443
;     mandatory=alpn,port
; )
